{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"744c1780-0647-4922-9d36-e2d7679e6ad3","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Why Session Replay Was Empty on the New UI\n\nIn `posthog_flutter`, setting `config.sessionReplay = true` in [`Analytics.init`](file:///tmp/h-dQGYOr/lib/analytics.dart#L4-L12) is not sufficient on its own for Flutter session replay—the root widget tree must also be wrapped in `PostHogWidget`, which mounts the `RepaintBoundary` and screenshot/masking capture layer needed to record Flutter frames.\n\n- [`LegacyApp`](file:///tmp/h-dQGYOr/lib/legacy_app.dart#L8-L25) wrapped `MaterialApp` in `PostHogWidget`, so session replays were recorded.\n- [`NewApp`](file:///tmp/h-dQGYOr/lib/new_app.dart#L19-L35) returned `MaterialApp.router` directly without `PostHogWidget`. Because `Posthog().setup(config)` and `PosthogObserver()` were still active, custom events and screen views arrived in PostHog, but no replay snapshots were captured.\n\n### Fix\n\n- Wrapped `MaterialApp.router` with `PostHogWidget` in [`NewApp.build`](file:///tmp/h-dQGYOr/lib/new_app.dart#L22-L34).\n- Added the root-cause analysis and fix details to [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-dQGYOr/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":138.015641,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":39531,"output_tokens":5046,"thinking_tokens":2871,"cache_read_tokens":157499,"total_tokens":44577}}}
